-Yes.

1218
00:57:45,068 --> 00:57:49,275
-If I stay until tomorrow,
will you go away with me?

1219
00:57:49,310 --> 00:57:50,620
-Where?

1220
00:57:50,655 --> 00:57:53,862
-To the sheriff, and then
after that away from here.

1221
00:57:53,896 --> 00:57:55,655
Maybe back to Austin with me.

1222
00:57:55,689 --> 00:58:00,137
-I can never leave them.
-Anyway, I hate line dancing.

1223
00:58:00,172 --> 00:58:02,724
-Why?
Why, Melissa?

1224
00:58:02,758 --> 00:58:05,586
-What happens to my family
is my responsibility.

1225
00:58:05,620 --> 00:58:07,724
-And why not Luther?
It's his family.

1226
00:58:07,758 --> 00:58:09,344
-You saw Lucinda
this afternoon.

1227
00:58:09,379 --> 00:58:14,206
She barely knows Molly or Lutheror anyone exists but me.

1228
00:58:14,241 --> 00:58:15,620
-Well.
-I saved her.

1229
00:58:15,655 --> 00:58:18,172
I'm the only one
that can reach her.

1230
00:58:18,206 --> 00:58:21,620
-I don't understand.
-Much of anything, really.

1231
00:58:23,793 --> 00:58:27,724
-Then stay.
Just one more day.

1232
00:58:27,758 --> 00:58:31,793
-Oh, you mean, "Stay!"
-All right.

1233
00:58:31,827 --> 00:58:36,068
-Ladies and gentleman, the most
malleable man in the world.

1234
00:58:36,103 --> 00:58:37,448
-I'll find a way.

1235
00:58:37,482 --> 00:58:40,655
-Come on, we'll have a nice,
murder-free walk.

1236
00:58:40,689 --> 00:58:42,551
-You really do believe
there's some...

1237
00:58:42,586 --> 00:58:44,448
-Bologna left.
-Oh, yeah.

1238
00:58:44,482 --> 00:58:48,655
-...some devil out there.
-Oh, yes.

1239
00:58:48,689 --> 00:58:53,344
-I've seen his food cake.
-I suppose that makes it true.

1240
00:58:53,379 --> 00:58:57,896
-It is true.
-Talk quicker!

1241
00:58:57,931 --> 00:59:01,896
-Just like those people
in the store.

1242
00:59:01,931 --> 00:59:05,344
They believe you're a witch,
so it's true for them.

1243
00:59:05,379 --> 00:59:07,034
Well, I don't, so you're not.

1244
00:59:07,068 --> 00:59:10,793
-Huh.
-I'm possessed by the devil.

1245
00:59:10,827 --> 00:59:14,137
-Michael Eisner?
-There's no such thing.

1246
00:59:14,172 --> 00:59:16,000
-I learned that
in community college.

1247
00:59:16,034 --> 00:59:17,310
-I heard his voice!

1248
00:59:17,344 --> 00:59:25,206
-He sang "Lend Me a Tenor."
-No, there is no devil.

1249
00:59:28,310 --> 00:59:31,000
-Oh.
-Brought to you

1250
00:59:31,034 --> 00:59:33,896
by the National Council
for Emergency Brakes.

1251
00:59:38,551 --> 00:59:40,482
-Didn't there used
to be a lake here?

1252
00:59:40,517 --> 00:59:42,241
-Damn.

1253
00:59:44,689 --> 00:59:46,620
-Lesson --
Never ask Kelsey Grammer

1254
00:59:46,655 --> 00:59:48,586
to get your gloves
out of your car.

1255
00:59:53,000 --> 00:59:55,413
-Now he's handcuffed
to the meatloaf.

1256
00:59:58,758 --> 01:00:00,344
-I just said the steak
was a little tough.

1257
01:00:00,379 --> 01:00:02,586
I didn't mean to
bring everyone down.

1258
01:00:05,758 --> 01:00:08,000
-Ah, so you're judging us now?

1259
01:00:11,448 --> 01:00:13,758
-You took too many pork chops.

1260
01:00:21,172 --> 01:00:23,000
-I saw a robin today.

1261
01:00:25,931 --> 01:00:28,586
-I could put my salad fork
right in his jugular.

1262
01:00:31,517 --> 01:00:33,241
-Well, I'm just going to stay
through the week.

1263
01:00:33,275 --> 01:00:36,620
Then that's it.

1264
01:00:36,655 --> 01:00:37,965
-I'll go lock myself
in the barn.

1265
01:00:38,000 --> 01:00:41,448
Don't get up.

1266
01:00:41,482 --> 01:00:44,758
-Honey, I found a deputy's
badge in my stew.

1267
01:00:44,793 --> 01:00:45,793
Oh.

1268
01:00:45,827 --> 01:00:51,241
♪♪

1269
01:00:54,793 --> 01:00:56,793
-Hmm, I need that Scottish guy

1270
01:00:56,827 --> 01:00:59,689
to come over and seal
up my windows.

1271
01:01:01,896 --> 01:01:06,172
-It must be hard getting whale
oil anymore for these lamps.

1272
01:01:06,206 --> 01:01:08,620
-Check it out,
she's dressed like Ed Ames.

1273
01:01:10,827 --> 01:01:13,965
Skiparoo.

1274
01:01:14,000 --> 01:01:16,103
-Dead rubber chicken,
what is that?

1275
01:01:18,103 --> 01:01:20,551
-Hmm.

1276
01:01:20,586 --> 01:01:23,206
-Time to go be a general
in the Michigan Militia.

1277
01:01:25,862 --> 01:01:28,103
-Oh, I made
a terrible sock monkey.

1278
01:01:28,137 --> 01:01:34,793
♪♪

1279
01:01:34,827 --> 01:01:38,068
-My obsession with the color
brown is getting out of hand.

1280
01:01:38,103 --> 01:01:43,551
♪♪

1281
01:01:43,586 --> 01:01:46,586
-Someone is playing the cicada
in the background.

1282
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:49,448
-Oh!
-Hey!

1283
01:01:49,482 --> 01:01:50,482
-Oh, my god.
-Ah!

1284
01:01:50,517 --> 01:01:51,517
-Oh, oh!
-Who is that?

1285
01:01:51,551 --> 01:01:52,517
-Oh.
-Hmm?

1286
01:01:52,551 --> 01:01:53,896
-Oh, yes.

1287
01:01:53,931 --> 01:01:56,344
-The editor got called out
of the room a lot I guess.

1288
01:01:58,241 --> 01:02:00,586
-I can't stop thinking
about that sandwich

1289
01:02:00,620 --> 01:02:01,793
I had the other day.

1290
01:02:01,827 --> 01:02:06,793
♪♪

1291
01:02:06,827 --> 01:02:08,896
♪ Do, do, do, Bernina

1292
01:02:08,931 --> 01:02:12,172
-It's the loneliest firefly
and his friends.

1293
01:02:15,379 --> 01:02:17,517
-Harpsichord is really
a stupid instrument.

1294
01:02:17,551 --> 01:02:18,551
-Oh.
-I'm sorry.

1295
01:02:18,586 --> 01:02:20,241
I'm in a bad mood.

1296
01:02:20,275 --> 01:02:26,241
-Oh, understood.
-Binding polymers and you.

1297
01:02:26,275 --> 01:02:28,310
-Burn the witch!
Burn the witch!

1298
01:02:28,344 --> 01:02:29,310
Burn the witch!

1299
01:02:29,344 --> 01:02:30,379
-Ah.
-Burn the witch!

1300
01:02:30,413 --> 01:02:32,000
-Burn the witch.
-Burn the witch!

1301
01:02:32,034 --> 01:02:33,448
Burn the witch!
Burn the witch!

1302
01:02:33,482 --> 01:02:35,068
-Oh, and go Packers too...
-Burn the witch!

1303
01:02:35,103 --> 01:02:37,551
-...but mostly burn the witch.

1304
01:02:37,586 --> 01:02:43,827
-The wicked man travaileth
with pain all his days.

1305
01:02:43,862 --> 01:02:48,620
-Said Madeline.
-And a number of years

1306
01:02:48,655 --> 01:02:51,827
is hidden to the oppressor.

1307
01:02:51,862 --> 01:02:52,965
-Bunch of crap.

1308
01:02:53,000 --> 01:02:55,103
-A dreadful sound
is in his ears.

1309
01:02:55,137 --> 01:02:56,758
-That's Paula Cole I think.
-Yes.

1310
01:02:56,793 --> 01:03:03,448
-Any prosperity, the destroyer
shall come upon him.

1311
01:03:03,482 --> 01:03:06,379
What is it, child?
-I heard something.

1312
01:03:06,413 --> 01:03:09,448
-Pay attention to
the word of God.

1313
01:03:09,482 --> 01:03:13,448
-For he loves you, and he may
kill you if you don't.

1314
01:03:13,482 --> 01:03:15,551
-Yea...
-Team.

1315
01:03:15,586 --> 01:03:19,793
-The light of the wicked
shall be put out...

1316
01:03:19,827 --> 01:03:21,034
-By 10:30.

1317
01:03:21,068 --> 01:03:25,655
-...and the spark of his fire
shall not shine.

1318
01:03:25,689 --> 01:03:27,551
-Just take the old-fashioned
photo, Dad.

1319
01:03:27,586 --> 01:03:31,586
-The light shall be dark
in his tabernacle...

1320
01:03:31,620 --> 01:03:32,793
-Mm.

1321
01:03:32,827 --> 01:03:36,965
-And his candle shall be
put out with him.

1322
01:03:37,000 --> 01:03:39,448
-Listen.
-Sit back, Lucinda.

1323
01:03:39,482 --> 01:03:42,068
-That's Aunt Eller.
-Ooh.

1324
01:03:42,103 --> 01:03:44,862
-They're coming for me.
-Calm yourself.

1325
01:03:44,896 --> 01:03:46,655
Sit back.

1326
01:03:48,793 --> 01:03:51,034
-So this family has been
pausing for centuries.

1327
01:03:51,068 --> 01:03:52,379
It's tradition.

1328
01:03:52,413 --> 01:03:57,000
-The steps of his strength
shall be straightened...

1329
01:03:57,034 --> 01:03:59,034
-Ah, this does drag,
doesn't it?

1330
01:03:59,068 --> 01:04:03,724
-And his own counsel...
-Mm-hmm.

1331
01:04:03,758 --> 01:04:05,413
-...cast him down...
-Burn the witch!

1332
01:04:05,448 --> 01:04:07,206
Burn the witch!

1333
01:04:07,241 --> 01:04:09,413
-...for he's cast...
-Out of plastic.

1334
01:04:09,448 --> 01:04:12,000
-Burn the witch!

1335
01:04:12,034 --> 01:04:13,827
Burn the witch!
Burn the witch!

1336
01:04:13,862 --> 01:04:15,275
-Yes?
-Burn the witch!

1337
01:04:15,310 --> 01:04:21,000
Burn the witch!
-...for he's cast into a...

1338
01:04:21,034 --> 01:04:22,310
-Yeah.
-...net...

1339
01:04:22,344 --> 01:04:24,137
-And it just goes
on from there.

1340
01:04:26,724 --> 01:04:28,034
-Oh.
Oh, that's right.

1341
01:04:28,068 --> 01:04:30,827
I called a service to come
around and burn my witch.

1342
01:04:30,862 --> 01:04:32,034
-What is it, David?

1343
01:04:32,068 --> 01:04:33,379
-It's people saying,
"Burn the witch."

1344
01:04:33,413 --> 01:04:36,103
Are you deaf?
-Burn the witch!

1345
01:04:36,137 --> 01:04:37,862
Burn the witch!
Burn the witch!

1346
01:04:37,896 --> 01:04:39,068
Burn the witch!

1347
01:04:39,103 --> 01:04:41,000
-Papa, what is it?

1348
01:04:41,034 --> 01:04:42,586
-People saying,
"Burn the witch."

1349
01:04:42,620 --> 01:04:44,793
Do you have any
deductive powers at all?

1350
01:04:44,827 --> 01:04:46,827
-I don't know yet.
-Burn the witch!

1351
01:04:46,862 --> 01:04:49,310
-Take your mother to the back
of the house...

1352
01:04:49,344 --> 01:04:50,758
-Work her over.

1353
01:04:50,793 --> 01:04:52,137
-And I'll see
what this is about.

1354
01:04:52,172 --> 01:04:53,241
-Burn the witch!

1355
01:04:53,275 --> 01:04:55,517
Burn the witch!
-It's pretty casual.

1356
01:04:55,551 --> 01:04:57,655
It's kind of like
a Lake Wobegon witch burning.

1357
01:04:57,689 --> 01:04:58,655
-Burn the witch!

1358
01:04:58,689 --> 01:05:01,551
Burn the witch!
-Burn the witch.

1359
01:05:01,586 --> 01:05:03,000
-Say, are you guys
burning witches?

1360
01:05:03,034 --> 01:05:08,448
Can I come?
-Big Hoss has lost some weight.

1361
01:05:10,379 --> 01:05:15,517
-Uh, we was out burning,
uh, uh, uh, uh... You tell him.

1362
01:05:17,827 --> 01:05:20,896
-Well, it seems
kind of silly now.

1363
01:05:20,931 --> 01:05:24,103
-Good evening, Mr. Keitel.

1364
01:05:24,137 --> 01:05:25,206
-Mr. Strickland.

1365
01:05:25,241 --> 01:05:27,758
-You've been hitting
the booze again.

1366
01:05:27,793 --> 01:05:32,551
-What can I do for you?
-Um, Mrs. Lucaster lost

1367
01:05:32,586 --> 01:05:35,965
her young one tonight,
only 3 years old.

1368
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:41,068
-Left her at Gymboree.
-I'm sorry to hear that.

1369
01:05:41,103 --> 01:05:44,034
-Kester Hagan here lost three
head of cow tonight,

1370
01:05:44,068 --> 01:05:46,413
and his wife is down sick.

1371
01:05:46,448 --> 01:05:47,827
-Hmm.
-I'm sorry.

1372
01:05:47,862 --> 01:05:52,000
-And my souffle fell today.
-It's a plague.

1373
01:05:52,034 --> 01:05:54,241
-I understand.
-Plague.

1374
01:05:54,275 --> 01:05:57,000
-The plague has hit near
everybody here,

1375
01:05:57,034 --> 01:05:59,068
David Strickland,
but it ain't hit you.

1376
01:05:59,103 --> 01:06:01,103
Now, how do you explain that?

1377
01:06:01,137 --> 01:06:05,689
-Well, I don't comb my hair
with rat bones.

1378
01:06:05,724 --> 01:06:07,310
-I can only assume...

1379
01:06:07,344 --> 01:06:12,379
-That I'm Franz Schubert.
-...that it's God's will.

1380
01:06:12,413 --> 01:06:15,137
-Don't talk to us about God,
David Strickland.

1381
01:06:15,172 --> 01:06:18,689
There's a witch in that house,
and we aim to have her.

1382
01:06:18,724 --> 01:06:21,413
-There is no witch
in that house.

1383
01:06:21,448 --> 01:06:22,413
-Well, my daughter
is kind of a witch,

1384
01:06:22,448 --> 01:06:23,620
but other than that, no witches.

1385
01:06:23,655 --> 01:06:25,965
-Go on home!

1386
01:06:26,000 --> 01:06:29,241
-We'll not go home until we get
what we come for.

1387
01:06:29,275 --> 01:06:32,206
Your daughter is a witch,
and she's put a hex on us!

1388
01:06:32,241 --> 01:06:37,034
-That's a damn fool thing
to say, Mr. Keitel.

1389
01:06:37,068 --> 01:06:39,862
Go on home.
-Ah, look at them go.

1390
01:06:39,896 --> 01:06:43,068
Run, you yellow-belly...
Oh, you're not.

1391
01:06:43,103 --> 01:06:46,000
-I'll talk to you tomorrow down
at Ben Proctor's store.

1392
01:06:46,034 --> 01:06:47,379
-There will be no talk.

1393
01:06:47,413 --> 01:06:49,000
We'll have the witch.

1394
01:06:49,034 --> 01:06:53,655
-Over my dead body!
-Uh-oh.

1395
01:06:53,689 --> 01:06:55,896
-So be it.
-Hmm.

1396
01:06:55,931 --> 01:06:58,103
-Come on.
-Smooth, Strickland.

1397
01:06:58,137 --> 01:06:59,103
-Lucinda, run!

1398
01:06:59,137 --> 01:07:00,551
Run!
Run!

1399
01:07:00,586 --> 01:07:03,689
-Oh, take my daughter, but
spare my commemorative plates!

1400
01:07:03,724 --> 01:07:04,965
-Oh, run, Lucinda, no!
-Ah!

1401
01:07:05,000 --> 01:07:06,827
Oh!

1402
01:07:06,862 --> 01:07:16,827
[Doors closing]

1403
01:07:16,862 --> 01:07:20,586
[Doors continue closing]

1404
01:07:24,793 --> 01:07:33,310
-[Speaking gibberish]
-Ah!

1405
01:07:33,344 --> 01:07:35,758
-Hey, hey, who are you?
Servo, stop it!

1406
01:07:35,793 --> 01:07:37,724
What are you doing?
Servo, heaven's sake!

1407
01:07:37,758 --> 01:07:39,000
-Bum, bum, buh, bum, bum,
dum, dum, hi, Mike.

1408
01:07:39,034 --> 01:07:41,310
What are you... What?
Grandma, darn it, Grandma!

1409
01:07:41,344 --> 01:07:43,413
Stop!
Now I told you, "No."

1410
01:07:43,448 --> 01:07:46,068
Jeez, I'm sorry, Mike.
-Wait a minute.

1411
01:07:46,103 --> 01:07:48,000
This is your grandma?
-It sure is, Mike.

1412
01:07:48,034 --> 01:07:49,068
Isn't she spry?

1413
01:07:49,103 --> 01:07:50,310
-When did you
get a grandma?

1414
01:07:50,344 --> 01:07:51,965
Ow, stay away.
-I have two grandmas, Mike.

1415
01:07:52,000 --> 01:07:53,206
I always have.

1416
01:07:53,241 --> 01:07:54,482
The other one doesn't
kill people though.

1417
01:07:54,517 --> 01:07:56,241
This one does.
That's how I tell them apart.

1418
01:07:56,275 --> 01:07:57,517
Ah, Grandma, down.
-Hey, hey.

1419
01:07:57,551 --> 01:07:59,655
-Down, Grandma.
-Oh, I guess it's okay.

1420
01:07:59,689 --> 01:08:01,517
I mean, couldn't you get her
a TV or something?

1421
01:08:01,551 --> 01:08:03,448
-Hold on a second.
What's that, Grandma?

1422
01:08:03,482 --> 01:08:06,275
Big, slow, tempting target?
Oh, believe me.

1423
01:08:06,310 --> 01:08:09,034
I know, but you just can't,
okay?

1424
01:08:09,068 --> 01:08:10,172
Well, I'll tell you what, Mike.

1425
01:08:10,206 --> 01:08:11,344
I'm just going to leave you
two alone

1426
01:08:11,379 --> 01:08:12,724
to start all over
with each other.

1427
01:08:12,758 --> 01:08:14,344
All right?
-No, Servo, don't.

1428
01:08:14,379 --> 01:08:15,586
-Oh, she's full of stories,
Mike!

1429
01:08:15,620 --> 01:08:18,689
Have a good time!
-Hey, hey, get away from me.

1430
01:08:18,724 --> 01:08:20,103
We'll be right back.

1431
01:08:20,137 --> 01:08:21,103
Back off, lady.

1432
01:08:21,137 --> 01:08:22,896
What?
What?

1433
01:08:22,931 --> 01:08:24,000
I'm sorry.
I didn't catch that.

1434
01:08:24,034 --> 01:08:26,034
What?
Ow, ow, hey, lady, stop it!

1435
01:08:26,068 --> 01:08:27,034
Stop it!
Stop!

1436
01:08:27,068 --> 01:08:29,172
Now back down, down, down!

1437
01:08:29,206 --> 01:08:34,586
♪♪

1438
01:08:35,482 --> 01:08:36,551
-Let go!
You're hurting me!

1439
01:08:36,586 --> 01:08:38,586
Let go of me!

1440
01:08:38,620 --> 01:08:41,517
-Ah, don't these people
have butter to churn

1441
01:08:41,551 --> 01:08:44,275
or taffy to pull,
prairie leagues to form?

1442
01:08:44,310 --> 01:08:46,206
-Something.
-Get off of me, no!

1443
01:08:46,241 --> 01:08:48,068
Please don't tie me up!

1444
01:08:48,103 --> 01:08:49,827
No, please stop!
-Please let me go!

1445
01:08:49,862 --> 01:08:51,137
-Quit whining.

1446
01:08:51,172 --> 01:08:55,620
-No, no, no, no!
-Help me!

1447
01:08:55,655 --> 01:08:58,241
Let me down from here!
-Oh, Neil Young.

1448
01:08:58,275 --> 01:09:00,413
-Oh, no, you're
making a mistake!

1449
01:09:00,448 --> 01:09:02,275
Help me!
Help me, Melissa!

1450
01:09:02,310 --> 01:09:06,275
-Hey, you been working out?
-Oh, no!

1451
01:09:06,310 --> 01:09:08,000
-You know, maybe if
the Amish used buttons,

1452
01:09:08,034 --> 01:09:09,758
they wouldn't be so irrational.

1453
01:09:09,793 --> 01:09:12,034
-No, no!

1454
01:09:12,068 --> 01:09:13,931
-Please, you're hurting me,
please!

